} | $2$ |  |\n| **D** | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our diagram.\n\n- There are $2$ arrows starting at Station A and ending at Station C. So, there are $2$ routes from A to C.\n\n- There are $2$ arrows starting at Station B and ending at Station A. So, there are $2$ routes from B to A.\n\n- There are no arrows starting at Station C and ending at Station C. So, there are no routes from C to C.\n\nTherefore, our route matrix is the following:\n\n|  |  | To: |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **A** | **B** | **C** | **D** |\n| From: | **A** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n| **B** | $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |  |\n| **C** | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $2$ |  |\n| **D** | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |  |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319412/field-1" "q-319412/field-2" "q-319412/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "10ca3efc-7d23-5bc1-ab41-f785bed69986"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
